{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q9H4H8","secondaryAccessions":["B4E1I7","Q5THR2","Q68EN1","Q6P457","Q7Z6H0","Q96DF5","Q96N89","Q9BVM8"],"uniProtkbId":"SCK1D_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2002-11-25","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2002-11-25","entryVersion":179,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Scaffolding CK1 anchoring protein D"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Protein FAM83D"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"}],"value":"Spindle protein CHICA"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:16122"}],"value":"SACK1D"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:16122"}],"value":"C20orf129"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:16122"}],"value":"FAM83D"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24344117"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25646692"}],"value":"Through the degradation of FBXW7, may act indirectly on the expression and downstream signaling of MTOR, JUN and MYC (PubMed:24344117). May play also a role in cell proliferation through activation of the ERK1/ERK2 signaling cascade (PubMed:25646692). May also be important for proper chromosome congression and alignment during mitosis through its interaction with KIF22 (PubMed:18485706)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22965910"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24344117"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24736947"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29789297"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"31338967"}],"value":"Interacts with FBXW7; promotes FBXW7 degradation (PubMed:24344117). May interact with RAF1 (PubMed:24736947). Interacts with KIF22; recruits KIF22 to mitotic spindle microtubules (PubMed:18485706). Interacts (via C-terminus) with DYNLL1 (PubMed:22965910). Interacts with HMMR (PubMed:22965910). Directly interacts (via SACK1 domain) with CSNK1A1 and CSNK1A1L (PubMed:29789297, PubMed:31338967)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9H4H8","intActId":"EBI-2556127"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P48729","geneName":"CSNK1A1","intActId":"EBI-1383726"},"numberOfExperiments":8,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9H4H8","intActId":"EBI-2556127"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O14576","geneName":"DYNC1I1","intActId":"EBI-366267"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9H4H8","intActId":"EBI-2556127"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O75330","geneName":"HMMR","intActId":"EBI-2556203"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"}],"value":"Primarily cytoplasmic during interphase, but at prophase, associates with spindle microtubules, with a clear concentration toward the spindle poles. It persists on spindle microtubules through metaphase and anaphase"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18445686"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29789297"}],"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18445686"}],"value":"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, spindle","id":"SL-0251"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15561729"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"}],"value":"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, spindle pole","id":"SL-0448"}}]},{"commentType":"ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS","events":["Alternative splicing"],"isoforms":[{"name":{"value":"1"},"isoformIds":["Q9H4H8-1"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Displayed"},{"name":{"value":"2"},"isoformIds":["Q9H4H8-2"],"sequenceIds":["VSP_036446"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Described"}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22965910"}],"value":"Expressed in the testis"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"}],"value":"Up-regulated during mitosis"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"29789297"}],"value":"All members of the SACK1 family of proteins share a conserved N-terminal DUF1669 (domain of unknown function 1669) domain of about 300 amino acids. This domain mediates the interaction with casein kinase 1 (CK1) isoforms. Therefore, it has been proposed to rename DUF1669 the scaffold anchor of CK1 domain (SACK1)"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18485706"}],"value":"Phosphorylated during mitosis"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"commentType":"DISEASE","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24344117"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24736947"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25646692"}],"value":"Probable proto-oncogene that regulates cell proliferation, growth, migration and epithelial to mesenchymal transition (PubMed:24344117, PubMed:24736947, PubMed:25646692). Expression increased in hepatocellular carcinoma, promotes proliferation and cell colony formation via activation of MEK/ERK signaling (PubMed:25646692). Expression increased in breast cancer; may be a prognostic indicator of poor disease-free survival (PubMed:24344117)"}]}},{"texts":[{"value":"Was named CHICA (girl in Spanish) because it interacts with KID"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the SACK1 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAH01068.2","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAH06553.3","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAH53683.1","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAH63661.1","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAH80188.1","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"BAB71016.1","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous termination","sequence":"BAB71016.1","note":"Truncated C-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXA